[h1]R.A.T.S. Cities and Borders[/h1]
[i]R.A.T.S. – Reconnaissance, Acoustics, Terrain & Signals[/i]

[b]The map of the day your mission starts.[/b]
Borders, capitals, cities and naval bases of the mission's date: the Soviet Union, two Germanys, Leningrad and Bonn, Holy Loch and Cam Ranh Bay.

[quote]▶ [b]Requires[/b] a mod loader: [b]R.A.T.S. Keel[/b] (Required items, top right) or Anchor Chain, either one
✉ Bugs, ideas, questions: [url=https://hub.sewerlabs.dev/s/borders]R.A.T.S. feedback board[/url]
⭐ A favourite helps other captains find it[/quote]

[h2]✦ New in 1.1[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]In the mission editor too,[/b] for the date you set there
[*][b]No double labels[/b] where the mission already marks a city
[*][b]Runs on the 3D globe[/b] (0.9.x) and the flat map (0.8.7)
[/list]

[h2]✦ Highlights[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Borders by date.[/b] The Soviet Union until 1991, two Germanys and West Berlin until October 1990, Yugoslavia, Czechoslovakia, two Yemens, the Vietnam DMZ
[*][b]Names of the time.[/b] East Berlin and Bonn, Leningrad, Gorky, Karl-Marx-Stadt, Bombay, Peking
[*][b]Naval bases with an anchor[/b] in their side's colour, only in the years they were used: Holy Loch until 1992, Cam Ranh Bay 1979-2002
[*][b]Air bases[/b] the same way
[*][b]Disputed lines dashed.[/b] Korea, Kashmir, the Golan, Cyprus
[*][b]Clean at every zoom.[/b] Lines keep their width, names don't overlap, a lighter set for the night map
[*][b]Coastal distance line[/b] at 3, 6 or 12 nm, off by default
[/list]

[h2]▶ Quick start[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe; Steam offers R.A.T.S. Keel with it if you have no mod loader
[*]Switch R.A.T.S. Cities and Borders on in Mods
[*]In a mission or the editor: map menu (≡), Map Layers, [b]Borders[/b] and [b]Cities and bases[/b]; or Shift+F7 and F7
[/olist]

[h2]⚠ Good to know[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Display only.[/b] No rules of engagement, triggers, zones or scoring change; units see and do the same
[*][b]A reference map, not the rules of your mission.[/b] Missions set their own areas (Map Layers, On Map Areas): go by the briefing, not by these lines
[*][b]Crossing a line[/b] is no violation unless the mission says so
[*][b]Simplified.[/b] Today's lines with date rules on top; land borders only, no sea borders or airspace; the Berlin Wall and the DMZ are hand-drawn
[*][b]The coastal line is a ruler,[/b] not a territorial limit: one distance for every country
[*][b]A base on the map[/b] doesn't mean the mission models it
[/list]

[h2]⚙ Where the data comes from[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Borders:[/b] [url=https://www.naturalearthdata.com/]Natural Earth[/url] 1:10m, public domain; which border existed when is my own work
[*][b]Cities, ports, airfields:[/b] the game's own lists, read from your install (nothing copied or shipped), plus Natural Earth places
[*][b]Naval bases with side and years:[/b] my own list, positions approximate
[*][b]Coastal line:[/b] worked out in the game from its own world grid
[*]Made with Natural Earth. Free vector and raster map data at naturalearthdata.com
[/list]

[h2]⚙ Settings[/h2]
[list]
[*][i]BepInEx\config\dev.sewerlabs.seapowerborders.cfg[/i]
[*][b]Borders:[/b] key, era (mission date or today), disputed lines, width, opacity, coastal line
[*][b]Cities:[/b] key, density, naval bases, air bases, civil airports, label size
[/list]

[h2]⚙ Install and game versions[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]R.A.T.S. Keel:[/b] https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3835527459
[*][b]Run in the game on 0.9.1[/b] (build 261112): Red Sea Breakout, under R.A.T.S. Keel
[*][b]0.8.7 (flat map):[/b] run with earlier versions; the right build switches on by itself, leave both DLLs in the folder
[*][b]No game files are changed.[/b] If an update breaks a hook, it says so in the log and stays out of the way
[*][b]More:[/b] [url=https://github.com/struckl/SeaPowerBorders]README on GitHub[/url]
[/list]

